Bullets can be safely enchanted by a blessed scroll of enchant weapon
when they are at +5 or lower, which will result in +6 or +7 bullets.
There is no real point in vaporizing any of them to try to get them up
to +8, and there isn't much point in getting them down to +5 (from +6)
for another shot at getting them up to +7.

I'm not sure if you can use a weapon shop's services to poison your
bullets, but if you can, it is surely worth the effort.  Be sure to
bless and rustproof your bullets too.  You might try polypiling blessed
poisoned arrows or darts to see if you can get poisoned bullets, if you
can't seem to obtain them any other way.  In any case, poisoned bullets
are not required, only a little extra cool.

Assault rifles have the highest useful fire rates (other than heavy
machine guns).  An assault rifle with a+5,+6, or +7 enchantment all
have the same fire rates.  If you have a huge surplus of assault rifles
and scrolls of enchant armor, you might try to get one up to +8, which
would have +1 to its maximum fire rate, but I don't think it is really
effective.

check the firearm spoiler at
http://glass.tvu.ac.uk/~chi/nethack/files/fire-648.txt for additional
details.

You might consider rings of increase damage - especially if they are
edible in your game (metal, wood, or bone).  Your increase damage bonus
is added to every shot.  If increase damage rings are edible in your
game, you might consider gypsy farming as a means of getting dozens of
rings that you can enchant up and devour.

Check the gypsy spoiler at
http://www.juiblex.co.uk/nethack/Shaligram/gypsy-006e4.txt for details
about getting wishes from gypsys.

Oh, and by the way, there is a method to wildly increase the level of
your worms, so that they will attack even the highest level monsters
without conflict.  Go down to the valley of the dead, and kill all the
non-wraiths - but don't kill the wraiths.  After that, bring your
purple worms down for a little dinner.  They should gain dozens of
levels.

